Description: skip Makefile-stripping rm when nodoc disables doc generation
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-06-02
Bug-Athena: libwmf's debian/rules execute_after_dh_installdocs-indep
 unconditionally runs `rm debian/libwmf-doc/usr/share/doc/libwmf-dev/doc/Makefile*`
 (and two deeper glob variants) to strip the autotools Makefiles
 that dh_installdocs would otherwise copy into the libwmf-doc
 binary alongside the doxygen-rendered HTML.
 .
 Under DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc the doc tree is never generated and
 dh_installdocs ships an empty libwmf-doc, so none of those three
 globs match.  Shell expands them to their literal pattern, `rm`
 returns "No such file or directory" for each, and exits 1 → build
 dies in binary-indep.
 .
 Fix: wrap the rm in `ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))`
 so the target no-ops cleanly when nodoc is active.  Behaviour
 without nodoc is unchanged.
 .
 TEMPORARY: nodoc is a workaround for missing doc-build tooling in
 the build pool, not a permanent policy.  DELETE THIS PATCH when
 CONF-08 lands and nodoc is dropped from [Source] BuildOptions /
 BuildProfiles in config/build.conf.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ execute_after_dh_install-arch:
 	ln -s libwmflite-0.2.so.7 debian/libwmf-dev/usr/lib/$(DEB_HOST_MULTIARCH)/libwmflite-0.2.so

 execute_after_dh_installdocs-indep:
+ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))
 	rm debian/libwmf-doc/usr/share/doc/libwmf-dev/doc/Makefile* \
 		debian/libwmf-doc/usr/share/doc/libwmf-dev/doc/*/Makefile* \
 		debian/libwmf-doc/usr/share/doc/libwmf-dev/doc/*/*/Makefile*
+endif
